WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.600
There’s no one definition to what makes
something a country.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.440
What decides if a country is a country essentially
is whether or not other countries agree that

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.130
the country is indeed a country.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:19.550
For this reason, counts of the number of countries
in the world range from 189-196.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:22.290
Each country decides which other countries
they recognize.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:26.869
If 100 UN member states suddenly recognized
your basement as it’s own country then it

00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:30.270
generally would be accepted that your basement
is it’s own country.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:33.960
There are, however, a number of steps that
any prospective country founder needs to take

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.520
if they want to have any shot at gaining international
recognition.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.160
Make a Claim
The first thing any one needs to begin creating

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.649
a country is a piece of land.

00:00:41.649 --> 00:00:43.350
One way to get it is to steal it.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.840
Of course, this involves having enough guns
to defend your territory.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.429
This would also be problematic for when your
country gets to the stage where it’s legitimacy

00:00:50.429 --> 00:00:54.929
is reviewed by other nations, but this method
has worked before.

00:00:54.929 --> 00:00:57.609
The easier method is to claim unclaimed land.

00:00:57.609 --> 00:01:01.651
However, with the advent of satellite imaging
and modern cartography there really are no

00:01:01.651 --> 00:01:05.160
islands or large pieces of territory that
are not known.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:10.390
Despite this, there is a small number of places
not governed or claimed by any recognized

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:11.450
government.

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:16.250
One of the better known recent claims happened
in an area unclaimed by both Croatia and Serbia

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.729
along the Danube river, the border between
the two countries.

00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:23.869
This micronation, known as Liberland, has
not received any international recognition

00:01:23.869 --> 00:01:28.860
and has been denounced by a number of nations,
but it still affirms it’s legitimacy based

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.500
off the lack of previous claim to it’s land.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.180
Its land is actually 17 times larger than
the land of the smallest recognized country,

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.540
the Vatican.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:41.969
Serbia did agree that Liberland did not infringe
upon it’s territory, but also dismissed

00:01:41.969 --> 00:01:44.380
the endeavor as “frivolous.”

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:47.880
Other new nations have had more success at
international recognition.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:51.590
Most of these are partially recognized nations
that split away from a more recognized state

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:53.719
with the backing of the people within the
territory.

00:01:53.719 --> 00:01:59.250
An example of this is South Ossetia, which
split away from Georgia in 1990 and currently

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:03.229
is recognized by Russia, Nicaragua, Venezuela,
and Nauru.

00:02:03.229 --> 00:02:08.729
Probably the best known and most hotly contested
recently formed nation is the State of Palestine.

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:14.180
136 nations recognize the Palestine and in
2012 it was designated by the United Nations

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:16.770
as a “non-member observer state.”

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.630
One other option for unclaimed land is Antartica.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:24.650
A large section of land known as the Marie
Byrd land has not been claimed by any recognized

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:25.860
nation.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.980
One issue with this option is the United Nations’s
“Antartica Treaty” which states that “No

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:34.780
new claim, or enlargement of an existing claim,
to territorial sovereignty shall be asserted

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.140
while the present Treaty is in force.”

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:42.080
There are claims that pre-exist this treaty
by seven different nations, although the legitimacy

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.750
of these claims is disputed given the treaty.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:50.090
In addition to the Antarctic Treaty issue,
establishing a sovereign nation in Antartica

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:52.730
would be difficult because of the next step
in the process.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:55.780
Establish a permanent population
A nation is created to serve it’s people,

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.480
and without people there is no nation.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.700
Antartica has no permanent population.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.760
There are always people in Antartica, but
these people do not constitute a permanent

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:07.770
population because they are primarily there
for research or tourism and none stay in Antartica

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.810
for more than a few years.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:14.570
Interestingly 11 babies have been born in
Antartica, but they generally have taken the

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:17.630
citizenship of their parents's country.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:21.320
A permanent population is one of the most
basic qualifiers for statehood.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:25.710
A sustainable independent nation would be
near impossible in Antartica.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:30.350
Any settlement would have no real economy
and no way to naturally produce food.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:35.460
However, there are talks of Antartica having
oil and, if this is the case, a sovereign

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:39.790
and potentially prosperous nation could be
established in the hostile environment, much

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:42.530
like the United Arab Emirates.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:47.150
Similar to the dozens of Antarctic micronation
claims, Liberland struggles with a lack of

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:48.760
permanent population.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:54.050
The founder’s attempts to re-enter the territory
have been blocked by both Serbia and Croatia.

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:58.230
At this point, it seems unlikely that a permanent
population will be established in the near

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:01.910
future and for this reason the future of Liberland
is bleak.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:05.181
3) Form a Government
A well formed government is probably the most

00:04:05.181 --> 00:04:09.230
important aspect dictating the success of
your new country.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:12.540
There are tons of forms of government, but
considering you’re forming this country

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:16.940
in the 21st century you’re likely to base
the government on John Locke’s principles

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.049
of government.

00:04:18.049 --> 00:04:23.419
Locke's principles essentially say that, in
nature, everybody has the right to “Life,

00:04:23.419 --> 00:04:26.330
health, Liberty, or Possessions.”

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:30.879
You might notice a similarity between this
and another famous document.

00:04:30.879 --> 00:04:35.560
According to Locke, in a natural society,
that is without a government, these rights

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:40.310
are not protected because there is no higher
power to do so, so in exchange for taking

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:45.170
away a part of these rights, for example liberty
when imprisoned or property when taxed, the

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:48.780
government acts to protect the very same rights.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:53.139
Locke also states that government only works
when there is a common belief in the abstract

00:04:53.139 --> 00:04:57.870
idea or illusion of government, and therefore
a government can only really exist when the

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:59.900
people are behind it.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:05.509
This is the reason that autocratic or absolutist
governments rarely work in modern society.

00:05:05.509 --> 00:05:09.530
So now keeping these principles in mind, you
need a constitution.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:13.729
Every single recognized country in the world
either has a constitution, or some substitution

00:05:13.729 --> 00:05:14.759
to it.

00:05:14.759 --> 00:05:18.889
This is not a complicated process, so I won’t
go into too much detail, but essentially any

00:05:18.889 --> 00:05:23.300
country must have a set of laws, principles,
and entities that make up the country and

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.080
the constitution works to define and specify
these.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.900
4) Gain International Recognition
This is where all you work comes under scrutiny.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:34.310
Gaining international recognition is by far
the most difficult step in the country creating

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.310
process.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:40.449
It takes potentially hundreds of years for
new countries to be fully or near fully recognized.

00:05:40.449 --> 00:05:44.319
Chances are that, unless you have overwhelming
backing from the people within your country,

00:05:44.319 --> 00:05:49.919
a good reason for the establishment of your
new nation, absolutely undisputed territory,

00:05:49.919 --> 00:05:54.360
and a well-balanced democratic government,
you won’t be recognized by any UN member

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:55.360
states.

00:05:55.360 --> 00:06:01.279
The chances of a new well recognized nation
outside of Africa or the Balkans is unlikely.

00:06:01.279 --> 00:06:05.919
The governments are too well-established or
stable outside of these areas.

00:06:05.919 --> 00:06:11.310
The final step to gain undisputed recognition
is to be admitted to the United Nations.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:16.259
Any application is reviewed by the security
council—composed of China, France, the Russian

00:06:16.259 --> 00:06:20.560
Federation, the United Kingdom of Great Britain
and Northern Ireland, the United States of

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.569
America, and a rotating group of 10 others.

00:06:23.569 --> 00:06:28.130
If 10 of the 15 vote in favor of your country,
congratulations, you’ve just joined the

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:29.130
United Nations!

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:31.479
By most metrics, you’re now a country.

00:06:31.479 --> 00:06:36.400
Of course, other United Nations members still
can fail to recognize you,and there are plenty

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:41.470
of UN member states that are not fully recognized,
however that’s a topic for another time.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:07:02.229
So good luck with your new country, thanks
for watching, and see you next time.

